1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,690
Welcome back to Equation Station SA!

2
00:00:02,960 --> 00:00:06,370
I'm Chris, and today I have a
question for you.

3
00:00:06,680 --> 00:00:11,250
In an exam, you factorise a quadratic
and find two critical values.

4
00:00:11,460 --> 00:00:14,170
But which values of x do you
actually choose?

5
00:00:14,480 --> 00:00:17,750
The numbers between them, or the
numbers outside them?

6
00:00:18,080 --> 00:00:22,840
Get that decision wrong, and even perfect
factorisation won't give you the correct

7
00:00:22,860 --> 00:00:27,680
final answer. Look at this inequality from a
twenty twenty six Western Cape

8
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:29,370
provincial Mathematics paper.

9
00:00:29,820 --> 00:00:31,450
We'll solve it together later.

10
00:00:31,860 --> 00:00:35,550
First, I want to show you a method that
makes your choice logical,

11
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:41,200
not a guess. In our previous Algebra lessons, we
solved equations by factorisation

12
00:00:41,220 --> 00:00:43,330
and with the quadratic formula.

13
00:00:43,660 --> 00:00:47,530
An equation might ask where a
quadratic expression equals zero.

14
00:00:47,780 --> 00:00:52,400
An inequality asks something different: where
is that expression greater than

15
00:00:52,420 --> 00:00:56,550
zero, less than zero, or possibly
equal to zero as well?

16
00:00:57,080 --> 00:01:01,330
Think about a graph. When the curve lies
above the horizontal axis,

17
00:01:01,540 --> 00:01:03,310
its y value is positive.

18
00:01:03,780 --> 00:01:06,630
Below that axis, its y value is negative.

19
00:01:06,880 --> 00:01:10,090
And exactly on the axis, its
value is zero.

20
00:01:10,600 --> 00:01:12,350
Here's a quick picture in your mind.

21
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:18,070
If I ask when a curve is BELOW the x axis,
I'm not asking for a single point.

22
00:01:18,260 --> 00:01:23,010
I'm asking for every x value across the part
of the graph that's below it.

23
00:01:23,120 --> 00:01:25,270
That's our whole big idea today.

24
00:01:25,460 --> 00:01:29,710
We'll use it to turn four symbols
greater than, less than,

25
00:01:29,820 --> 00:01:34,240
greater than or equal to, and less than or
equal to into correct answers on

26
00:01:34,260 --> 00:01:38,760
a number line. Let's start with a real three
mark question from the Mpumalanga

27
00:01:38,780 --> 00:01:42,470
June twenty twenty six Grade twelve
Mathematics Paper One.

28
00:01:42,940 --> 00:01:46,990
Solve x squared plus five x, less
than or equal to zero.

29
00:01:47,440 --> 00:01:49,030
The first step is familiar.

30
00:01:49,340 --> 00:01:51,390
Take out the common factor, x.

31
00:01:51,580 --> 00:01:56,710
We get x multiplied by x plus five,
less than or equal to zero.

32
00:01:57,080 --> 00:02:01,930
To find our critical values, we temporarily
ask when the product equals zero.

33
00:02:02,200 --> 00:02:06,840
That happens when x equals zero, or
when x plus five equals zero,

34
00:02:06,860 --> 00:02:09,410
which gives x equals negative five.

35
00:02:09,820 --> 00:02:13,120
Be careful here. These are the
boundaries of our answer,

36
00:02:13,140 --> 00:02:15,710
not automatically the entire answer.

37
00:02:16,240 --> 00:02:18,970
Place negative five and zero
on a number line.

38
00:02:19,180 --> 00:02:23,990
They divide all real numbers into three
regions: left of negative five,

39
00:02:24,160 --> 00:02:27,410
between negative five and zero,
and right of zero.

40
00:02:27,840 --> 00:02:30,650
Imagine a road divided by two signposts.

41
00:02:31,040 --> 00:02:34,780
A point on one stretch tells us the sign
everywhere on that stretch,

42
00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:38,910
because the polynomial can change sign
only where it crosses zero.

43
00:02:39,360 --> 00:02:42,050
Now let's test one number in each region.

44
00:02:42,320 --> 00:02:44,690
To the left, choose negative six.

45
00:02:45,360 --> 00:02:48,950
Negative six multiplied by negative
one is positive six.

46
00:02:49,160 --> 00:02:52,390
Between the critical values,
choose negative two.

47
00:02:52,820 --> 00:02:56,750
Negative two multiplied by positive
three is negative six.

48
00:02:57,020 --> 00:02:59,530
To the right, choose positive one.

49
00:02:59,840 --> 00:03:02,930
One multiplied by six is positive six.

50
00:03:03,180 --> 00:03:06,670
Listen to that pattern: positive,
negative, positive.

51
00:03:07,300 --> 00:03:11,170
The question wants the expression to be
less than or equal to zero.

52
00:03:11,340 --> 00:03:14,850
So we choose the middle region, where
the expression is negative.

53
00:03:15,280 --> 00:03:20,120
And because the question says or equal to, we
also include both critical values,

54
00:03:20,140 --> 00:03:22,790
where the expression is exactly zero.

55
00:03:23,060 --> 00:03:27,340
Our final answer is: x is greater than
or equal to negative five,

56
00:03:27,360 --> 00:03:29,790
and less than or equal to zero.

57
00:03:30,100 --> 00:03:35,230
We can also write x belongs to the closed
interval from negative five to zero.

58
00:03:35,580 --> 00:03:38,290
Now watch the same answer
appear on a graph.

59
00:03:38,780 --> 00:03:41,790
Draw y equals x squared plus five x.

60
00:03:42,060 --> 00:03:46,920
The parabola opens upward and crosses the
horizontal axis at negative five and

61
00:03:46,940 --> 00:03:51,390
zero. Between those crossings, the
curve dips below the axis.

62
00:03:51,860 --> 00:03:54,670
Outside them, the curve rises above it.

63
00:03:54,720 --> 00:03:58,670
So the number line, the sign test
and the graph all agree.

64
00:03:58,880 --> 00:04:01,850
We are not shading the space
inside the parabola.

65
00:04:01,980 --> 00:04:06,690
We are identifying the x values for which
its height is on or below zero.

66
00:04:07,020 --> 00:04:08,690
That's an important difference.

67
00:04:09,020 --> 00:04:11,170
Here's another way to test
what you're seeing.

68
00:04:11,560 --> 00:04:16,200
Put your finger at x equals negative two on
the horizontal axis and move up

69
00:04:16,220 --> 00:04:18,390
or down until you meet the curve.

70
00:04:18,540 --> 00:04:24,050
You land below zero. At x equals one, the
curve sits above the axis.

71
00:04:24,340 --> 00:04:26,670
The visual check agrees with
the arithmetic.

72
00:04:27,140 --> 00:04:31,610
Here's the question I want you to keep asking:
where is the expression positive,

73
00:04:32,040 --> 00:04:36,090
where is it negative, and what does the
inequality actually request?

74
00:04:36,420 --> 00:04:40,280
Let me flip the situation with a four mark
question from the Free State June

75
00:04:40,300 --> 00:04:42,390
twenty twenty six Paper One.

76
00:04:42,740 --> 00:04:46,630
Solve x squared plus two x minus
three, greater than zero.

77
00:04:47,120 --> 00:04:50,840
Factorise to get x plus three
multiplied by x minus one,

78
00:04:50,860 --> 00:04:55,770
greater than zero. The critical values are
negative three and positive one.

79
00:04:55,900 --> 00:04:57,690
Now test each interval.

80
00:04:58,160 --> 00:05:02,700
Choose negative four on the left: negative one
times negative five is positive

81
00:05:02,720 --> 00:05:08,210
five. Choose zero in the middle: three times
negative one is negative three.

82
00:05:08,640 --> 00:05:13,130
Choose positive two on the right: five
times one is positive five.

83
00:05:13,380 --> 00:05:16,830
Again, the signs are positive,
negative, positive.

84
00:05:17,160 --> 00:05:20,570
But this time the question asks
for greater than zero.

85
00:05:20,660 --> 00:05:23,430
That means we want the two
outside regions.

86
00:05:23,720 --> 00:05:26,970
If you're tempted to choose the middle
because you see the two roots,

87
00:05:27,320 --> 00:05:30,760
remember that zero lies in the middle, and
the expression there is negative

88
00:05:30,780 --> 00:05:34,890
three. It cannot satisfy a greater
than zero inequality.

89
00:05:35,220 --> 00:05:41,130
The answer is: x is less than negative
three, OR x is greater than one.

90
00:05:41,400 --> 00:05:42,890
Did you notice something else?

91
00:05:43,160 --> 00:05:46,540
The Free State question uses a
strict greater than sign,

92
00:05:46,560 --> 00:05:48,330
without an equal sign.

93
00:05:48,440 --> 00:05:51,330
That means the two critical
values are excluded.

94
00:05:51,660 --> 00:05:53,990
We use open circles on the number line.

95
00:05:54,140 --> 00:05:59,620
Why? Because if you substitute x equals
negative three or x equals one,

96
00:05:59,640 --> 00:06:02,090
the expression is exactly zero.

97
00:06:02,300 --> 00:06:04,870
And zero is NOT greater than zero.

98
00:06:04,980 --> 00:06:09,850
But in our Mpumalanga question, less than or
equal to included the boundaries,

99
00:06:09,940 --> 00:06:11,790
so we used closed circles.

100
00:06:12,020 --> 00:06:13,500
And listen to the final language.

101
00:06:13,520 --> 00:06:18,010
When we select a connected interval,
such as negative five to zero,

102
00:06:18,060 --> 00:06:22,630
we say x is at least negative
five AND at most zero.

103
00:06:22,900 --> 00:06:27,820
When we select two separate outside regions,
we say x is less than negative

104
00:06:27,840 --> 00:06:30,250
three OR greater than one.

105
00:06:30,460 --> 00:06:33,930
Don't change AND into OR just
because you are rushing.

106
00:06:34,040 --> 00:06:37,430
Those words represent completely
different sets of numbers.

107
00:06:37,636 --> 00:06:42,069
Now it's your turn with the Western Cape
Cape Winelands May and June twenty

108
00:06:42,089 --> 00:06:44,246
twenty six Paper One question.

109
00:06:44,616 --> 00:06:46,086
It's worth four marks.

110
00:06:46,736 --> 00:06:52,856
Solve x squared minus five x plus four,
minus ten, greater than or equal to

111
00:06:52,876 --> 00:06:57,666
zero. Before I show you the solution,
pause and try three things.

112
00:06:58,156 --> 00:06:59,426
Simplify the expression.

113
00:06:59,756 --> 00:07:01,526
Find the critical values.

114
00:07:01,636 --> 00:07:05,526
Then decide whether you need the
middle or the outside regions.

115
00:07:05,786 --> 00:07:07,766
Give yourself a real attempt.

116
00:07:08,156 --> 00:07:11,506
If you write down only the two roots
without choosing regions,

117
00:07:11,536 --> 00:07:13,406
your answer is not finished.

118
00:07:13,756 --> 00:07:15,786
Ready? Let's mark it together.

119
00:07:16,316 --> 00:07:17,966
First combine the constants.

120
00:07:18,616 --> 00:07:21,246
Positive four minus ten is negative six.

121
00:07:21,396 --> 00:07:27,406
So we have x squared minus five x minus six,
greater than or equal to zero.

122
00:07:27,896 --> 00:07:33,276
Now factorise. We need two numbers with
product negative six and sum negative

123
00:07:33,296 --> 00:07:37,806
five. Those numbers are negative
six and positive one.

124
00:07:38,056 --> 00:07:42,736
The expression becomes x minus six,
multiplied by x plus one,

125
00:07:42,756 --> 00:07:44,966
greater than or equal to zero.

126
00:07:45,496 --> 00:07:48,386
The critical values are six
and negative one.

127
00:07:48,656 --> 00:07:50,526
In the middle, choose zero.

128
00:07:51,076 --> 00:07:54,176
Negative six times positive one
gives negative six,

129
00:07:54,196 --> 00:07:56,206
so the middle does not work.

130
00:07:56,596 --> 00:08:01,026
On the left of negative one and the right of
six, the product is positive.

131
00:08:01,176 --> 00:08:02,726
That's where we need to be.

132
00:08:03,036 --> 00:08:07,046
Because equality is allowed, both
boundary values are included.

133
00:08:07,516 --> 00:08:11,456
Our final answer is: x is less than
or equal to negative one,

134
00:08:11,476 --> 00:08:15,106
OR x is greater than or equal to six.

135
00:08:15,576 --> 00:08:17,406
Compare that with your own answer.

136
00:08:17,656 --> 00:08:18,886
Did you simplify first?

137
00:08:19,236 --> 00:08:21,146
Did you choose the outside intervals?

138
00:08:21,496 --> 00:08:23,086
Did you include the endpoints?

139
00:08:23,496 --> 00:08:26,746
Those are exactly the decisions
the memorandum rewards.

140
00:08:27,336 --> 00:08:30,686
Here's one trap I want to fix before
you write another exam.

141
00:08:31,356 --> 00:08:36,096
Suppose the question says negative x squared
plus three x plus four is greater

142
00:08:36,116 --> 00:08:37,786
than or equal to zero.

143
00:08:38,136 --> 00:08:41,346
You might prefer a positive
coefficient of x squared.

144
00:08:41,416 --> 00:08:46,086
That's fine. But if you multiply the
entire inequality by negative one,

145
00:08:46,276 --> 00:08:48,480
the inequality sign MUST reverse.

146
00:08:48,500 --> 00:08:54,570
We get x squared minus three x minus four,
less than or equal to zero.

147
00:08:55,100 --> 00:08:59,140
Factorise it as x minus four,
multiplied by x plus one,

148
00:08:59,160 --> 00:09:01,330
less than or equal to zero.

149
00:09:01,600 --> 00:09:04,650
The critical values are
negative one and four.

150
00:09:04,976 --> 00:09:09,196
Since the expression opens upward, it is
negative between those values,

151
00:09:09,216 --> 00:09:12,126
and equality allows us to
include the endpoints.

152
00:09:12,656 --> 00:09:16,536
The correct answer is: negative one is
less than or equal to x,

153
00:09:16,556 --> 00:09:19,626
and x is less than or equal to four.

154
00:09:19,976 --> 00:09:23,946
Let's verify that using x equals zero
in the original expression.

155
00:09:24,256 --> 00:09:29,596
Negative zero squared plus zero plus four is
four, which is greater than or

156
00:09:29,616 --> 00:09:33,926
equal to zero. And zero lies inside
our chosen interval.

157
00:09:33,996 --> 00:09:39,996
Now test x equals five: negative twenty five
plus fifteen plus four is negative

158
00:09:40,016 --> 00:09:43,546
six, so five must NOT be in our solution.

159
00:09:43,876 --> 00:09:46,916
The checks agree. If you forget
to reverse the sign,

160
00:09:46,936 --> 00:09:49,086
you will select the wrong region.

161
00:09:49,356 --> 00:09:53,486
And one more thing: never assume the
middle is always negative.

162
00:09:53,736 --> 00:09:57,756
That quick pattern applies to our upward
opening examples with two distinct

163
00:09:57,776 --> 00:10:02,546
roots. A sign test or an accurate
graph is the reliable method.

164
00:10:02,756 --> 00:10:04,746
One last question before we finish.

165
00:10:05,456 --> 00:10:08,446
Solve x squared minus nine,
less than zero.

166
00:10:08,756 --> 00:10:11,436
Pause for a moment and decide
which interval works.

167
00:10:11,456 --> 00:10:16,516
We can factorise it as x minus three,
multiplied by x plus three,

168
00:10:16,536 --> 00:10:21,606
less than zero. The critical values are
negative three and positive three.

169
00:10:21,736 --> 00:10:26,316
Try zero in the middle: zero squared
minus nine gives negative nine,

170
00:10:26,336 --> 00:10:27,776
which is less than zero.

171
00:10:27,796 --> 00:10:29,946
So the middle interval is correct.

172
00:10:30,176 --> 00:10:32,066
But the inequality is strict.

173
00:10:32,556 --> 00:10:35,006
Negative three and three are excluded.

174
00:10:35,296 --> 00:10:40,596
The final answer is: x is greater than
negative three AND less than positive

175
00:10:40,616 --> 00:10:44,266
three. If you got that right, you've
understood the method.

176
00:10:44,636 --> 00:10:47,386
Now you've got a process you can
use in a new question,

177
00:10:47,556 --> 00:10:50,406
even if the roots or the
inequality symbol change.

178
00:10:50,696 --> 00:10:54,536
Let's finish with four steps you can use in
your next Mathematics Paper One

179
00:10:54,556 --> 00:10:58,706
question. First, put the
inequality into standard form.

180
00:10:59,016 --> 00:11:04,126
Second, factorise or use another valid
method to find the critical values.

181
00:11:04,496 --> 00:11:08,106
Third, test the signs or inspect
an accurate graph.

182
00:11:08,436 --> 00:11:12,876
Fourth, write the correct intervals, including
the endpoints only when equality

183
00:11:12,896 --> 00:11:16,306
is allowed. Remember, don't
just find the roots.

184
00:11:16,576 --> 00:11:19,506
Find the x values that satisfy
the inequality.

185
00:11:19,776 --> 00:11:23,626
For more practice, visit Equation
Station SA dot top.

186
